title: Let a reap sweep skip a busy ticket instead of stopping
created: 2026-09-24T22:57:48Z
updated: 2026-09-24T22:57:48Z
effort: S
area: cli
handoff:

In the tracker-wide sweep (bin/pidly:800-807), reap_one runs inside the
`map | while` subshell and dies when it cannot take a ticket's lock. die
exits that subshell, so `|| true` never runs and the sweep stops at the
first contended ticket. reap_one should return nonzero and the sweep should
carry on, the way cmd_fields handles lock failure.
